 law. The tally was 61-16, so the No share is about 21%, well above the 10% near-unanimous line.\n- **Timing:** the vote falls in her current Assembly term, so it counts as `in-term`.\n- **Why it seats rung 2:** the bill is single-subject. Its Section 220.5 says a school \"shall not enact or enforce any policy, rule, or administrative regulation that would require an employee or a contractor to disclose\" a pupil's gender identity \"to any other person without the pupil's consent.\" That matches rung 2 clause for clause.\n- **Why not rung 1:** Section 220.3 only says staff \"shall not be required\" to disclose. It never requires staff to keep the information from parents, which is what rung 1 needs.\n- **Evidence:** the chair rests on the bill text, which carries the provision quote, and on the vote page, which carries the line naming her and the tally. Both are one record on the same bill, so code should compute the evidence tier as single-source.\n- **Nothing outstanding:** there are no quotes (no source has her own words) and nothing in `needs_source`.\n\nThe Assembly's earlier floor vote, on 2024-04-25, was on a different text about school health services. I did not rely on it.","ttft_ms":8616,"type":"result","duration_ms":27117,"uuid":"e9251630-7a9e-4228-af12-10158d4e5b0c","ttft_stream_ms":1378,"time_to_request_ms":204,"first_content_frame_ms":1379,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
